  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...The weekend will begin with drier, cooler, and breezy \nconditions in the wake of a departing low pressure system. \nWinds will diminish with temperatures moderating some for \nSunday.\n\nThe initial weaker cold front is continuing to move offshore\nthis evening with the precipitation gradually tapering off into\nearly tonight. A secondary cold front moves through overnight\nwhich will help usher in cooler air for this weekend as a\nsurface low pressure system departs to the northeast.\n\nFor this weekend, there will be an upper-level closed low that will\nbe slowly approaching from the Great Lakes region into the\nNortheast. During the day Saturday, this closed low will move \neastward right through our forecast area by later in the day. \nMeanwhile, low pressure at the surface will deepen as it pulls \neast of New England. The gradient between this low, and high \npressure towards the center of the country, will result in a \nbreezy day in addition to cooler temperatures compared to our \nrecent warmth. Generally expect highs for Saturday in the upper \n50s to around 60 with it feeling even cooler with the breeze. \nExpect west to WNW winds around 10-15 gusting up to 25 mph. The \nday should overall feature a mix of sun and clouds with a few \nshowers possible across the southern Poconos due to the upper \nlow moving through and the tail end of some lake effect to the \nnorth and west. \n\nHeading into the second half of the weekend, the upper-level \nlow departs to the north and east as shortwave ridging moves in.\nThe pressure gradient also relaxes some as the surface low pull\nfarther away into Atlantic Canada. This will result in a \nlighter breeze with slightly warmer temperatures compared to \nSaturday and a mainly clear to partly cloudy sky. Expect highs \nSunday mainly in the low 60s following morning lows mainly \nranging from the upper 30s to mid 40s. \n\nGenerally dry and fair weather looks to dominate for early through \nmid next week.",
